# Build-context rules for deploy/docker/Dockerfile (BuildKit reads this file
# because it sits beside the Dockerfile and is named <Dockerfile>.dockerignore).
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs an explicit list, so this file is the SECOND wall, not the
# first: it keeps the corpus and secrets from being SENT to the daemon at all,
# and keeps the context small enough to build quickly.
#
# ANCHORING. A pattern with a leading path (`eval/sets`, `deploy`) matches only at
# the context ROOT. `**/x` matches at any depth. That distinction is deliberate:
#   * repo layout   code is at the root; vault-derived eval material is at eval/
#   * archive       code is under app/ and the CORPUS is at the root (data/,
#                   rag_data/) -- the owner's own eval sets, shipped on purpose
#                   under app/eval/, are therefore NOT matched by the root-
#                   anchored lines and stay in.

# ---- secrets and the live personal config ---------------------------------
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/secrets.env
**/*.key
**/*.pem
# The container's config is a MOUNTED file (generated by make_docker_config.py).
# The checkout's own config.yaml carries machine paths and the live settings.
**/config.yaml
**/config.docker*.yaml

# ---- the corpus and everything derived from it ------------------------------
# data/ holds the JSONL chunk files (primary data); rag_data/ the indexes.
**/data
**/rag_data
**/chroma_db
**/*.jsonl
**/*.pkl
**/*.sqlite3
**/logs
**/*.log

# ---- vault-derived evaluation material (repo layout) -----------------------
# Question sets, bench run records and seed packs quote the vault.
eval/sets
eval/runs
eval/seeds
eval/*.json
eval/*.md

# ---- not part of the runtime image ------------------------------------------
.git
.github
.claude
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
# deploy/ is excluded PIECE BY PIECE, not as a folder: the Dockerfile COPYs three
# files out of deploy/docker (constraints.txt, docker-entrypoint.sh,
# healthcheck.sh), and a file the context does not contain cannot be copied.
# tests/test_deploy_assets.py simulates this matching to keep it that way.
deploy/k8s
deploy/package
deploy/README.md
deploy/docker/Dockerfile*
deploy/docker/docker-compose*.yml
deploy/docker/make_docker_config.py
deploy/docker/.env.example
docs
landing
tests
ocr-sidecar
embed-sidecar
models
site
_recovery
.release-staging
# Session notes and one-off scripts
HANDOFF*.md
WORKLOG.md
CLAUDE.md
INSTRUCTIONS.md
_verify_*.py
_check_*.py
check_*.py
